&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Chainguard is the trusted source for open source. By delivering hardened, secure, and production-ready builds of all the open source software engineers and AI agents rely on, Chainguard helps organizations build faster, stay compliant, and eliminate risk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our customers include Fortune 500 enterprises and global industry leaders, including Anduril, Canva, Fortinet, Hewlett Packard Enterprise, OpenAI, Snap Inc., and Snowflake. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Chainguard is venture-backed by leading investors, including Amplify, IVP, Kleiner Perkins, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Mantis VC, Redpoint Ventures, Sequoia Capital, and Spark Capital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chainguard is the trusted source for open source. By delivering hardened, secure, and production-ready builds of all the open source software engineers and AI agents rely on, Chainguard helps organizations build faster, stay compliant, and eliminate risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include Fortune 500 enterprises and global industry leaders, including Anduril, Canva, Fortinet, Hewlett Packard Enterprise, OpenAI, Snap Inc., and Snowflake.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chainguard is venture-backed by leading investors, including Amplify, IVP, Kleiner Perkins, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Mantis VC, Redpoint Ventures, Sequoia Capital, and Spark Capital.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role, in a nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chainguard Containers is our core product, and this team builds it. As a Senior Software Engineer in Container Product Engineering you will design and ship the features, services, and build systems behind Chainguard Containers, working in a small sub-team of two to four engineers that owns one project end to end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chainguard is growing explosively. Every line of code is now written with AI in the loop, which means the foundation it runs on has to be secure by default. You will build that foundation: the hardened container images, the registry that serves them, and the tooling that lets engineers and AI agents adopt them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a product role. You will work directly with Product Managers and customers, make the trade-off calls on the features you own, and ship them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What the team owns&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product features for Chainguard Containers.&lt;/strong&gt; Letting customers push their own images to our registry, Custom Assembly (customers compose images from our hardened packages), Helm charts, notifications, and compliance views such as STIG dashboards (STIG is the US government&#39;s hardening standard).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The image build pipeline.&lt;/strong&gt; The systems that turn packages from Wolfi, our Linux distribution, into signed and attested container images at scale, including moving image builds onto our own runner infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Registry performance and distribution.&lt;/strong&gt; Work such as lazy loading, so a container starts before its whole image has downloaded, and image signing with Sigstore.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adoption tooling for engineers and AI agents.&lt;/strong&gt; Migration tools that convert existing Dockerfiles to Chainguard Containers, and MCP servers (Model Context Protocol, the standard that lets AI agents call tools) so agents can discover and pull our images directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and ship new features and services for Chainguard Containers, from a one-page design through production and the first week of customer use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the trade-offs on your work: scope, sequencing, what to cut, and when &quot;good enough to ship&quot; beats &quot;complete&quot;. Say so clearly when a plan is at risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with AI coding agents as part of how you build, review, and operate, and help the team raise the bar on how it uses them safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow a problem wherever it goes: into another team&#39;s service, a customer call, a support ticket, or go-to-market data, rather than stopping at the edge of your own repository.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the systems you touch healthy: observability, on-call, and the fixes that stop the same page from coming back.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clearly and often. Design notes, pull request descriptions, and status updates are how a remote team moves fast together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years building and operating software that paying customers use, preferably at a startup or a company in hyper-growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency and urgency. You find a way, you do not wait to be unblocked, and you ask for help early when you are stuck.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Judgment on trade-offs. You can explain why you chose speed here and rigor there, and you can change your mind when the data says to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems thinker. You reason about how a change moves through the build pipeline, the registry, and the customer&#39;s cluster, and you anticipate what breaks next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native in how you work. You use agentic coding tools daily and can show what changed in your output because of them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity. You can pick up a half-defined problem, decide what to build, and pivot when priorities shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong fundamentals in a systems language (Go preferred), API design, databases and caching, and cloud infrastructure on GCP or AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of containers, container registries, the OCI image format (Open Container Initiative, the standard for container images and registries), and Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low ego. You do what you say and say what you do, and you communicate early when the news is bad.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written English and experience working on a distributed, remote-first team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software supply chain security background: SBOMs (software bill of materials), Sigstore signing, or SLSA (Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts, a framework for build integrity).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Chainguard&#39;s open-source tools: Wolfi, apko, and melange.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Terraform or other infrastructure-as-code experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author of or contributor to open-source projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A non-traditional path into engineering. We value people who learned by building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remote. United States preferred; Open to Canada, the United Kingdom, and Germany. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or relocation for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explore Our Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dive into the practical side of what we do at Chainguard. These resources provide a hands-on look at our processes and offer an opportunity for in-depth understanding of our product offerings and the technology behind them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://edu.chainguard.dev/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Chainguard Academy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chainguard.dev&quot;&gt;https://www.chainguard.dev&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$157,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$184,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We live and breathe our company values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are customer obsessed — We focus on delivering solutions to our customers that create value and make their lives better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have a bias for intentional action — We prioritize, plan, try things, and fail fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We don&#39;t take ourselves too seriously (but we do serious work) — We are solving an important problem which takes focus, but we also like to enjoy the journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We trust each other and assume good intentions — We&#39;re transparent with decisions to empower team members to make well informed decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A few of the benefits we offer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible &amp;amp; Remote-First Culture:&lt;/strong&gt; Work remotely with team meetup opportunities, bi-annual destination summits, and a monthly stipend for coworking spaces, phone and internet costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Approach to Equity:&lt;/strong&gt; Receive stock options upon hire and promotion. Plus, you can participate in secondary offerings and have 10 years to exercise your options (yes, you read that correctly: 10 years!).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;100% Covered Health Insurance:&lt;/strong&gt; We cover 100% of your health, vision and dental insurance premiums for you and your dependents. Nothing comes out of your paycheck.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;∞ Flexible Time Off:&lt;/strong&gt; Take the time you need – to do our best work, we need to recharge and reset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;18 Weeks Paid Parental Leave:&lt;/strong&gt; We offer 18 weeks for birthing parents and 12 weeks for non-birthing parents, with the option to use it all at once or throughout your child&#39;s first year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If your experience is close but doesn&#39;t fulfill all requirements, please apply. We&#39;re building the best team in technology and are focused on hiring &quot;Chainguardians&quot; with unique backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chainguard is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you acknowledge that Chainguard will process your personal data in accordance with &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chainguard.dev/legal/candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Chainguard&#39;s Global Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;©2026 Chainguard. All Rights Reserved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;fabric-text-color-mark&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-text-custom-color=&quot;#36b37e&quot;&gt;IDnow is a&lt;strong&gt; leader in digital identity and fraud prevention in Europe&lt;/strong&gt; with a mission to transform trust into the most powerful asset in the digital world, empowering enterprises with &lt;strong&gt;AI-driven, SaaS-based identity solutions that deliver scalable security, adaptive compliance, and real-time fraud prevention&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;fabric-text-color-mark&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-text-custom-color=&quot;#36b37e&quot;&gt;Through its broad portfolio of digital identity and fraud prevention solutions, IDnow establishes, maintains and enriches trust throughout the customer journey, ensuring businesses can confidently and securely operate while leveraging digital identity to drive growth, security and scalability. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;fabric-text-color-mark&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-text-custom-color=&quot;#36b37e&quot;&gt;The company has &lt;strong&gt;offices in Germany, United Kingdom, Romania and France&lt;/strong&gt;, and is backed by renowned institutional investors, including Corsair Capital and Seventure Partners. Its &lt;strong&gt;portfolio of international clients spans a wide range of end markets&lt;/strong&gt; including financial services, telecommunications, travel &amp;amp; mobility, gaming, and other industries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position is based in Rennes, France.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Solutions Engineer at IDnow is the &lt;strong&gt;client&#39;s trusted advisor through pre-sales and integration&lt;/strong&gt;. You design the solution the client will rely on, you give them confidence that it will work in their environment, and you become the person they turn to for technical and solution decisions. &lt;strong&gt;Your focus is the technical side of the journey up to the point where the client is live on our products, and you make that path smooth&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a &lt;strong&gt;hands-on, deeply technical role, and a commercial one&lt;/strong&gt;. Solutions Engineers carry a quota and are measured on two things: the deals they help win, and whether the client goes live successfully. &lt;strong&gt;You work hand in hand with Sales &lt;/strong&gt;to convince the client that our solution is the right one and to move them toward signature, and then you make sure they can use it well in production. You earn that through technical depth, but you are client-facing, credible and persuasive in a sales motion. You do this across our whole client base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We hire this role at more than one level. The core of the job is the same; the scope you own and the complexity you handle grow with your experience. This role carries real ownership across the client journey, and a say in how the work evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div data-testid=&quot;markdown-response&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Discover and Design&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical discovery, qualifying conversion rates, false acceptance and rejection trade-offs, fraud exposure and integration constraints before proposing a solution,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design end-to-end solution architectures that orchestrate document verification, digital identity, fraud signals, biometric authentication, eID and EU Digital Identity Wallet flows, and e-signature,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Link every technical choice to the client’s business objectives and Key Performance Indicators (KPIs), so proposals speak to outcomes rather than features,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define defensible architecture decisions covering fallback logic, data residency, scalability and performance,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Sales with proposals, Requests for Proposal (RFPs) and Requests for Information (RFIs), advising on which capabilities to combine and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Prove, Integrate and Go Live&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead proof-of-concept and pilot engagements, configuring Application Programming Interface (API) integrations, building Postman collections and managing sandbox environments,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate behaviour under realistic conditions and document what the client needs to go live,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide client developers through API and mobile Software Development Kit (SDK) integration, including webhooks, authentication and testing,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot integration issues by reading logs and diagnosing failures at the API and SDK level, rather than only forwarding them,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a living integration map of the client’s architecture, data flows and dependencies,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the account from signature to go-live, running the go-live plan and handing a documented account to Customer Success and Support at the end of hypercare.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Advise and Enable&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted advisor relationships with business and technical stakeholders, from first conversation to go-live,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the client’s technical reality internally, feeding integration blockers, product gaps and pilot learnings back to Product and Sales teams,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the internal escalation team on deeper platform issues, arriving with clear technical context,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand alongside Sales in client meetings, addressing objections on integration effort, feasibility and alternatives,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve demo environments, architecture templates and integration guides, and mentor team members as the practice grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;container-element section-element editable-element section_with_title-element-57a6ed87-9a65-412d-b52c-7002d3fb072d section_with_title-element-default-section-with-title&quot; data-v-51f33a98=&quot;&quot; data-v-fd08594a=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;container-element section-element editable-element section_with_title-element-7525b616-170d-49ba-8189-de0a0bb7b01f section_with_title-element-default-section-with-title&quot; data-v-51f33a98=&quot;&quot; data-v-fd08594a=&quot;&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;editable-element-layer&quot; data-v-607a5d63=&quot;&quot; data-v-422f1a2b=&quot;&quot; data-v-fd08594a=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;text-element editable-element editable-text-element&quot; data-v-fd08594a=&quot;&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;text-element-header_text-2&quot;&gt;Preferred Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You ask before you propose and qualify before you demo, turning ambiguous client requirements into the right technical solution. You take ownership of the client’s technical path from first conversation to production, and you explain complex systems in plain language to engineers and business leaders alike. You combine hands-on engineering depth with a commercial mindset, and you enjoy working alongside Sales to move a decision forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering or technical degree&lt;/strong&gt;, a Master’s degree in a relevant field, or equivalent practical experience,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3+ years of experience in solutions engineering, technical consulting, or implementation and onboarding in SaaS&lt;/strong&gt;, ideally in identity, FinTech or security,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery and qualification skills&lt;/strong&gt;, with the ability to turn an ambiguous client requirement into the best technical solution,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution architecture skills&lt;/strong&gt;, including designing integration flows, explaining orchestration logic and defending trade-offs with a client’s engineers,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on technical skills&lt;/strong&gt; with APIs, Software Development Kits (SDKs) including &lt;strong&gt;mobile, and integration tooling&lt;/strong&gt; such as Postman and Git,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running a proof of concept and debugging an integration at the API or log level,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery discipline to run an integration and onboarding through to a committed go-live date, managing several client projects at once,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to translate technical complexity into plain language and reassure non-technical stakeholders,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business value awareness&lt;/strong&gt;, connecting the technical solution to client outcomes such as verification conversion, fraud loss or time to go-live,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client-facing presence, building trusted advisor relationships with business stakeholders such as Chief Digital Officers (CDOs) and Heads of Digital, and technical stakeholders such as Chief Technology Officers (CTOs), architects and platform engineers,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The instinct to own the client’s technical path end to end,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent English and full professional French are both hard requirements for the role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Additional European languages are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with identity verification, Know Your Customer (KYC), Know Your Business (KYB) or Anti-Money Laundering (AML) processes, including document verification, biometrics, liveness detection, eID and fraud detection,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in where digital identity is heading, including eIDAS 2.0, EU Digital Identity Wallets, the EU Anti-Money Laundering Regulation and General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR),&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile SDK delivery on iOS, Android or React Native,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of web development concepts, including frontend and backend architecture, webhooks and Open Authorisation (OAuth),&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in mobility, FinTech, banking or other regulated industries,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of a programming language such as Python, Java or JavaScript, and of a cloud platform such as Amazon Web Services (AWS), Microsoft Azure or Google Cloud Platform (GCP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Perks &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellbeing:&lt;/strong&gt; Use your full access to the mental health platform &lt;em&gt;nilo&lt;/em&gt;, including 1on1 sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We value&lt;strong&gt; personal and professional development:&lt;/strong&gt; make full use of &lt;em&gt;Udemy&lt;/em&gt;, our training platform with 24/7 access and unlimited content/course consumption incl. certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We make your &lt;strong&gt;remote work comfy:&lt;/strong&gt; we provide support on equipment and offer flexible working hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We value collaboration &amp;amp; love to come together: regular&lt;strong&gt; onsite gatherings, internal initiatives&lt;/strong&gt; and summer parties to connect outside of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;May your family require your attention or other reasons apply: use the benefit of our&lt;strong&gt; paid &lt;/strong&gt;special&lt;strong&gt; leave days.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy the possibility to combine work with a longer stay at your holiday destination or extend a weekend with our&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Workcation possibilities.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to the perks &amp;amp; benefits above, we offer &lt;strong&gt;specific benefits that differ between our locations.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
