&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTRE ENGAGEMENT EN FAVEUR DE L&#39;INCLUSION ET DE L&#39;ACCESSIBILITE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez Decathlon, nous reconnaissons l&#39;immense valeur qu&#39;apporte la diversité à nos équipes et nous nous efforçons continuellement de favoriser et de cultiver un lieu de travail inclusif et équitable : c&#39;est pourquoi l&#39;Inclusion est l&#39;un de nos Fondamentaux Humains. Nous encourageons les personnes de tous horizons et de toutes capacités à postuler, car nous sommes convaincu·es que la diversité des pensées, des cultures, des identités et des expériences vécues nous rend plus fort·es.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decathlon s&#39;engage également à offrir un processus de sélection inclusif et accessible à tous les candidat·es. En cas de besoin d&#39;aménagement, tu peux en faire la demande via le formulaire de candidature, celle-ci sera confidentielle. Ces demandes n&#39;affectent pas le résultat du processus de recrutement&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Imaginez si la technologie nous permettait de repousser les frontières et d&#39;offrir des expériences sportives inédites. C&#39;est précisément notre ambition chez Decathlon Digital ! Nous sommes une équipe de plus de 5 000 experts en ingénierie logicielle, gestion de produits, données, cloud et cybersécurité, répartis à Paris, Lille et Amsterdam. Ensemble, nous créons la plus vaste plateforme sportive numérique, en exploitant les innovations technologiques pour optimiser la chaîne de valeur, concevoir des expériences connectées et donner une seconde vie à nos produits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changeons la donne pour de bon.&lt;/strong&gt; Notre passion du sport nous guide et nous voulons qu’elle perdure. C’est pourquoi nous nous engageons à bâtir un modèle technologique plus durable, en réduisant notre impact direct sur l&#39;environnement, et en créant un espace sûr et inclusif pour apprendre et nous épanouir ensemble. Rejoins l’équipe et façonnons le futur du sport.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time position for 8 months to cover maternity leave.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Brand &amp;amp; Communication Senior Manager, you will be responsible for implementing the Demand Generation communication strategy and roadmap. You will own the conception and supervise the development of communication activities, including brand campaigns (online and offline), social media activities, PR &amp;amp; events, focusing on increasing the efficiency of the campaigns and making sure it perfectly reflects the brand positioning.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will focus on creating impactful and creative campaigns, working closely with both local and global resources, and analyse and report the performance of these activities on a regular basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will manage different stakeholders at a local level, including a Junior communication manager and a Copywriter, as well as the different agencies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will coordinate with different local marketing teams to perfectly operate the plan, like the Influencer team or the Online Paid team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also be in regular contact with international stakeholders to align on the implementation of the campaigns, share best practices and gather useful consumer insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a Management position. It requires strong management skills, as well as strong project management and coordination skills, due to the broad nature of the projects. You will work hand in hand with the Brand &amp;amp; Communication Director, being her direct report.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owner of the development of Demand Generation brand activities, including brand campaigns (online and offline), chef partnership, social media and PR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the conception, planning, production and report of the brand activities, liaising with a wide range of stakeholders (including the Global Brand Team, Agencies, Local marketing teams) and ensuring that we deliver a quality result on time and on budget. Brand activities include a broad nature of projects such as video campaigns, offline campaigns, brand partnership campaigns, organic social media, stunts…&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse campaign performance and channel results; generate actionable insights and optimisations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the main point of contact for other local teams, working together on on-brand communications for all touchpoints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage our local Brand Campaign Manager and Copywriter, as well as drive the Creative Agency and Social Media agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who are you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years experience in communication/brand project management in a B2C scale up/eCommerce brand or top communication agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brand mindset: you are passionate about brands, creative advertising and marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset: you analyse the performance of your work and generate actionable learnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative mindset: you like working with different stakeholders, with a solution-driven attitude,&amp;nbsp; with strong people and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage different projects, with efficient processes, respect of deadlines and budget conscience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous, organised, proactive and adaptable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English and French - both written and spoken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will you get?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dynamic, international environment with a strong company culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A supportive, passionate, proactive and dynamic French team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offices in the heart of Paris, in the 1st arrondissement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hybrid setup combining remote work and time in the office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perks: HelloFresh discounts, Swile meal vouchers, Gymlib access, transport benefits, and everything else that makes coming to the office great&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our recruitment process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;ll review your profile. If it&#39;s a match, we&#39;ll invite you to a series of interviews and a case study. We&#39;re committed to scheduling interviews quickly so we can welcome you to HelloFresh as soon as possible!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your start at HelloFresh:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you join, we&#39;ll cook up onboarding sessions that let you meet every manager and get a real feel for how HelloFresh works. You&#39;ll also have time to get to know your team better before diving into your responsibilities!&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is a global data and AI consulting firm. We help organisations turn data and AI into measurable business impact across the value chain, from strategy and operating model to data platforms, AI products and marketing. More than 2,500 consultants, data scientists and engineers work for over 1,000 clients worldwide, including Samsung, L’Oréal, Orange and Sanofi.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Switzerland, our team of around 50 people works from Zurich and Lausanne with Swiss and international companies. Our work covers AI strategy and governance, data transformation and AI use cases that run in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing: Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Partner to scale Artefact’s Pharma &amp;amp; Life Sciences practice in Switzerland. Many global pharma, biotech and medtech companies run their headquarters, R&amp;amp;D, manufacturing or commercial functions from Switzerland. We already work with life sciences clients here and now want to make this practice one of the pillars of our Swiss business. This is an origination role: most of your time goes into winning new clients and expanding existing relationships. You will be based in Zurich and work with clients across Basel, Zurich and Romandie.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your role will encompass:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaling the Swiss Life Sciences practice: its offer, its client base and its team, in coordination with Artefact’s global healthcare and life sciences teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growing existing client relationships and winning new clients, so that the practice moves from first references to a broad portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading senior client stakeholders (CDO/CDAO, CIO, heads of Commercial Excellence, Medical Affairs, R&amp;amp;D Operations, Manufacturing &amp;amp; Quality) through data and AI transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overseeing project delivery and quality assurance on our life sciences engagements, and giving strategic support to ongoing client programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sparring with the Swiss Managing Partner on practice strategy and investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Among your responsibilities as Partner, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the practice and its offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build on our existing life sciences work to define where data and AI create value along the pharma value chain: R&amp;amp;D and clinical development, regulatory and medical affairs, manufacturing and quality, supply chain, and commercial engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate this into a few Swiss offers with clear entry points, scope and pricing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop the client portfolio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a go-to-market plan for Swiss life sciences, own the pipeline and write proposals that address the client’s actual problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate pharma procurement: vendor qualification, framework agreements and preferred-supplier panels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver to the highest standard&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sponsor and oversee engagements run day to day by Engagement Managers, with multidisciplinary teams of consultants, data scientists and data/AI engineers, and ensure the quality of what we deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure delivery meets regulatory requirements: GxP, validation of AI systems, Swiss FADP/GDPR and the EU AI Act.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for client satisfaction, project margin and team experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop our knowledge base&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Speak and publish on AI in life sciences, for example GenAI in medical and regulatory writing, AI in clinical operations, HCP engagement, and AI governance under GxP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn our Swiss life sciences work into references and case studies, and bring them into Artefact’s global practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and develop the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and develop consultants with life sciences experience, train the wider Swiss team on the domain, and own staffing on your engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12–15 years of experience, including 8+ years serving pharma, biotech or medtech clients at a life sciences–focused consultancy or the life sciences practice of a strategy or technology firm. A later move in-house is welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently Director, Principal or Associate Partner with a personal sales target, ready for the step to Partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of origination with life sciences clients: you can name clients you opened yourself and the revenue you sold, beyond extending existing accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A network among decision-makers in the Swiss life sciences industry, especially in Basel and Zurich, that you are actively growing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of GxP and computer system validation, and how they apply to data and AI systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working fluency in data and AI: you can discuss what an AI use case needs from data, what it costs and when it pays back.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English. German is a strong advantage, French a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in or willing to relocate to the Zurich area, with regular travel to Basel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape what comes next: the Swiss practice has proven itself and is growing fast. It is still small enough that you shape its clients, its offers and its team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell with a global platform: you bring the credentials, delivery capacity and AI assets of a 2,500-person firm into every proposal, and you work with industry leads across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy to production under one roof: our consultants and engineers work in the same teams, so your clients get from recommendation to working solution without changing firms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture: innovation, collaboration and action shape how we work. Artefact Switzerland is Great Place to Work certified (2026).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurship: you are measured on the clients, revenue and team you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

